          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='3778' hidden='true' id='20' story-point-id='8' type-v2='text' w='31250' x='5188' y='15667'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#252525' fontname='Roboto' fontsize='18' lmargin='555' rmargin='555'>Top 10 closest encounters with Earth</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18' lmargin='555' rmargin='555'>Æ&#10;</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='34111' hidden='true' id='21' story-point-id='8' type-v2='text' w='17750' x='81625' y='52222'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='16'>These are the most critical passes — all of these objects passed at a distance of less than 15,000 km from Earth. Nearest: 2020 VT4 (6,746 km)</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='21889' hidden='true' id='22' story-point-id='9' type-v2='text' w='27188' x='61563' y='22444'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>The increase in the number of detected hazardous objects does not mean that there are more of them — it just means that we are seeing them better. However, the number of ‘Close’ and ‘Very Close’ encounters is constantly increasing.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='20222' hidden='true' id='23' story-point-id='10' type-v2='text' w='35063' x='62250' y='68111'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#252525' fontname='Tableau Regular'>Objects classified as &apos;hazardous&apos; are not necessarily the fastest every year, but they have consistently high speeds. The trend shows a slight decrease in non-hazardous objects, but not in dangerous objects.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='49556' id='24' story-point-id='11' type-v2='text' w='14500' x='83625' y='21222'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>The largest detected Near-Earth Objects vary significantly by year, with diameters ranging from 1 km to over 13 km.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>The cumulative trend shows a sharp increase after 2000, driven by advances in telescope technology and expanded survey coverage.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='19889' id='25' story-point-id='11' type-v2='text' w='14563' x='83688' y='71333'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>The continuous growth in detected NEOs highlights the importance of planetary defense and sustained monitoring efforts.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{B4832731-912F-4D01-A8B8-00F757F1A6BB}' />
    </dashboard>
  </dashboards>
